Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["One-loop graviton self-energy", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"2df07368-cefb-4f42-98b1-c8a7694a579e"],

Cell["\<\
Build the pure-gravity tadpole, graviton bubble and ghost bubble, reduce them \
to scalar integrals, and compare the combined tensor with a spin-projector \
representation.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b996e84f-dcf3-4586-ab3e-c3d7381cad31"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Setup and notation", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"470c3ee4-e85e-4e4b-8f19-289b9456293e"],

Cell["\<\
Start with a fresh Mathematica kernel and evaluate the input cells from top \
to bottom (Shift+Enter). Install FeynGrav and its FeynCalc dependency first; \
see the package README. Opening this notebook executes nothing. A semicolon \
stores an intermediate result without printing its full expression. Use \
?FunctionName for help and FeynGravCommands[] to discover the package \
interface.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3143437a-b563-4895-a8ea-617e4800b851"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"<<", "\"\<FeynGrav`\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{4.000099225160284*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3694a769-13d0-4dbf-894a-06e2b6f7a788"],

Cell["\<\
This example requires FORM on the kernel PATH. CalcFormCalculate performs \
bosonic algebra and Lorentz contractions, using TFORM automatically when \
available. TID then performs the loop reduction. The named integrand and \
contracted expression make it possible to inspect either stage separately.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9780ed65-e14f-441f-98a8-4ab291583ca5"],

Cell["\<\
The external momentum is p, the loop momentum is k, and m denotes the matter \
mass where present. Repeated Lorentz or colour indices are summed. TID[..., k, \
ToPaVe -> True] reduces tensor integrals to scalar A0 and B0 functions. In \
FeynCalc\[CloseCurlyQuote]s convention these expressions retain the i \[Pi]\
\.b2 normalisation; no (2\[Pi])^(-D) loop-measure prefactor is inserted here. \
Keep D symbolic during reduction. Setting D -> 4 in a displayed coefficient \
is not a Laurent expansion, UV subtraction, or a renormalised answer.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6b28079f-0abb-4ccb-9f93-73b4e3383df2"],

Cell["\<\
FeynGrav supplies the vertex and propagator normalisations, including i and \
\[Kappa]. The default gravitational gauge parameter is GaugeFixingEpsilon = \
2. The displayed diagram weights are retained from the original example; the \
notebook does not derive their combinatorics.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dfa2dcc2-d0dd-4903-98e8-157860b2469c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2. Massless tadpole", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f10855b8-2bf8-4d4d-a419-3aebc934453d"],

Cell["\<\
The four-graviton vertex closes into one massless propagator. In dimensional \
regularisation the resulting scaleless tadpole vanishes. This is why its \
combinatorial weight does not affect the subsequent non-zero sum.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000099291450745*^9, 
  4.000099297480855*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"aba65d18-7af1-46b8-a4ee-\
993500861f22"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"TID", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"CalcFormCalculate", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"GravitonVertex", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "p", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", 
        
        RowBox[{"-", "p"}], ",", "\[Rho]", ",", "\[Sigma]", ",", 
        RowBox[{"-", "k"}], ",", "\[Lambda]", ",", "\[Tau]", ",", "k"}], 
       "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"GravitonPropagator", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "\[Rho]", ",", "\[Sigma]", ",", "\[Lambda]", ",", "\[Tau]", ",", "k"}],
        "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "k", ",", 
    RowBox[{"ToPaVe", "->", "True"}]}], "]"}], "==", "0"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000099262806889*^9, 4.000099294633368*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[2]:=",ExpressionUUID->"0c0bfdd4-617d-43a2-85d6-4218cea0b538"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3. Graviton bubble", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b0d5f114-3795-40ec-913d-b25814bb73b0"],

Cell["\<\
Connect two cubic vertices with propagators of momenta k and p-k. \[Mu],\[Nu] \
and \[Alpha],\[Beta] are free external index pairs. TID performs the one-loop \
tensor reduction; ToPaVe -> True retains scalar Passarino\[Dash]Veltman \
functions. The factor 1/2 is applied in the final sum, not in this definition.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"84098caa-c57f-40b4-9645-02c8dee8dd74"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"PolarizationOperator1", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "\[Mu]_", ",", "\[Nu]_", ",", "\[Alpha]_", ",", "\[Beta]_", ",", "p_"}], 
     "]"}], "=", 
    RowBox[{"Collect", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"TID", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"CalcFormCalculate", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"GravitonVertex", "[", 
           RowBox[{"\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "p", ",", "m1", ",", "n1", ",", 
            RowBox[{"-", "k"}], ",", "a1", ",", "b1", ",", 
            RowBox[{"-", 
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"p", "-", "k"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"GravitonPropagator", "[", 
           RowBox[{"m1", ",", "n1", ",", "m2", ",", "n2", ",", "k"}], "]"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"GravitonPropagator", "[", 
           RowBox[{"a1", ",", "b1", ",", "a2", ",", "b2", ",", 
            RowBox[{"p", "-", "k"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"GravitonVertex", "[", 
           RowBox[{"m2", ",", "n2", ",", "k", ",", "a2", ",", "b2", ",", 
            RowBox[{"p", "-", "k"}], ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", 
            RowBox[{"-", "p"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "k", ",", 
        RowBox[{"ToPaVe", "\[Rule]", "True"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"A0", "[", "__", "]"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"B0", "[", "__", "]"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"C0", "[", "__", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "Factor"}], "]"}]}], 
   ";"}], "//", "AbsoluteTiming"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0000993289385567`*^9, 4.000099354979412*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[3]:=",ExpressionUUID->"81fafd12-10bc-4e3e-b838-94e107a56085"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["4. Gravitational ghost bubble", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f4b287c6-673c-490d-b822-d057386e5c56"],

Cell["\<\
The leading minus sign is the closed ghost-loop sign. The two factors of i \
and the massless FAD denominators are explicit in this integrand.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"eb792614-1a14-4e4c-b53b-ffa29232f087"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"PolarizationOperator2", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "\[Mu]_", ",", "\[Nu]_", ",", "\[Alpha]_", ",", "\[Beta]_", ",", "p_"}], 
     "]"}], "=", 
    RowBox[{"Factor", "[", 
     RowBox[{"TID", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"CalcFormCalculate", "[", 
        RowBox[{"-", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"GravitonGhostVertex", "[", 
            RowBox[{"\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "p", ",", "a", ",", 
             RowBox[{"-", "k"}], ",", "m", ",", 
             RowBox[{"-", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"p", "-", "k"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"GravitonGhostVertex", "[", 
            RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", 
             RowBox[{"-", "p"}], ",", "n", ",", 
             RowBox[{"p", "-", "k"}], ",", "b", ",", "k"}], "]"}], " ", 
           SuperscriptBox["\[ImaginaryI]", "2"], " ", 
           RowBox[{"MTD", "[", 
            RowBox[{"a", ",", "b"}], "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"MTD", "[", 
            RowBox[{"m", ",", "n"}], "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"FAD", "[", 
            RowBox[{"k", ",", 
             RowBox[{"p", "-", "k"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}], "]"}], ",", "k", ",", 
       RowBox[{"ToPaVe", "\[Rule]", "True"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "//", 
  "AbsoluteTiming"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000099384012746*^9, 4.000099394906754*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[4]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f1643c19-062d-4eec-8fe8-c448cceefdfe"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5. Assemble the operator", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ee8825ea-1126-4f3d-8225-ffc3f1b4fed6"],

Cell["\<\
Combine one half of the graviton bubble with the ghost bubble, using the \
original example\[CloseCurlyQuote]s weights. No external propagators are \
attached.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6d1b48eb-10a9-42a7-996f-8f0aa30f871c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"PolarizationOperator", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "\[Mu]_", ",", "\[Nu]_", ",", "\[Alpha]_", ",", "\[Beta]_", ",", "p_"}], 
     "]"}], "=", 
    RowBox[{"Factor", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       FractionBox["1", "2"], " ", 
       RowBox[{"PolarizationOperator1", "[", 
        RowBox[{
        "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p"}], 
        "]"}]}], "+", 
      RowBox[{"PolarizationOperator2", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p"}], 
       "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "//", "AbsoluteTiming"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000099403387553*^9, 4.000099405697338*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[5]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3001fd45-846c-44cb-974e-b38fdfb23923"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["6. Extract and reconstruct the projector form", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1ebedf0a-041d-4faf-9876-ebb297142bbc"],

Cell["\<\
The coefficients below are extracted from the tensor calculated above using \
the installed package. The reconstruction check tests this decomposition; it \
is not an independent check of the loop calculation. The older hard-coded \
expression is omitted because it does not match the current vertex rules.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6e34d4d7-21cb-4b12-9770-ddd749f1e968"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gravitonProjectorCoefficients", "=", 
   RowBox[{"Factor", "/@", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"NieuwenhuizenOperatorExpansion", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"PolarizationOperator", "[", 
         RowBox[{
         "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p"}], 
         "]"}], ",", "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",",
         "p"}], "]"}], "/.", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
      RowBox[{"D", "\[Rule]", "4"}]}], ")"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[6]:=",ExpressionUUID->"9756eb19-cad5-4c67-92a5-9c185e6eaebf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Grid", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<P1\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<P2\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<P0\>\"", ",",
         " ", "\"\<P0Bar\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<P0BarBar\>\""}], "}"}], ",", 
      " ", "gravitonProjectorCoefficients"}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Alignment", " ", "->", " ", "Left"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[7]:=",ExpressionUUID->"694e6e15-5a3b-43aa-9048-cd086e13ff04"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gravitonProjectorForm", "=", 
   RowBox[{"NieuwenhuizenOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sequence", "@@", "gravitonProjectorCoefficients"}], ",", 
     "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p"}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[8]:=",ExpressionUUID->"27aac17d-3afd-4fcb-8cf9-ec039c258b24"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"CalcFormCalculate", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"PolarizationOperator", "[", 
        RowBox[{
        "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p"}], 
        "]"}], "-", "gravitonProjectorForm"}], "]"}], "/.", 
     "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     RowBox[{"D", "\[Rule]", "4"}]}], ")"}], "\[Equal]", "0"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000099419025693*^9, 4.000099423773789*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[9]:=",ExpressionUUID->"c43c817e-e9a0-43c5-9f75-707134a51c69"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["How to adapt this example", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"539a15c4-b172-4b90-842a-2af02c1fcd25"],

Cell["\<\
Change one ingredient at a time: a mass, a momentum assignment, or a vertex \
order. Restart the kernel before rerunning with different kinematics, because \
scalar-product definitions and assumptions persist in the session. \
Re-evaluate all dependent cells after a change. Inspect the stored \
intermediate expressions if a comparison is False or remains unevaluated; do \
not treat an unresolved expression as a passed check.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7efe82c3-c90d-4471-92c9-cf0b8d461105"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
},
